// A VIEW HELD ACROSS A BLOCK (F and P of landing 177a; management_12's rulings of 2026-11-01 10:55 and 11:18). The two statement kinds that hold a header value across a block, each with no party until this landing:
// F, `for`: `for (uint8:b in string_bytes(s)) { s = string_concat("wx", "yz"); n = n + (b => int64); }` read freed bytes (44, 229, 98 on 175 and 176b). The loop's iterable, a call's result or a range, is a party of the loop's frame now (`f*`, `h3*`). `f14_move` gives two reports, BORROW-015 and MOVE-001: the post-180 list.
// P, a lending `pick`, both spellings: a direct write in the arm was TYPE-067, but a write through a held pointer, a holder or a pointer parameter changed the variant under the binding. `q9_wild_ptr`, `q10_wild_param`: MachineFault at 0x41414141, a fabricated pointer in safe code (97, the worst exit of the family);
// the other writers OutOfBounds (98) or a freed string (89). An arm that BINDS A NAME raises a view party on the selector's place, live for the arm. STATEMENT FORM: `q*`, `p3`, `p5`, `p7`, `pf_field_sel`, `pl_elem_sel`, `pz_nested`. EXPRESSION FORM: `px*`. An arm that binds nothing raises none (the twins, `block_held_view_ok.npk`).
// OVER-REFUSED ON PURPOSE, THE POST-180 LIST: a write through a POINTER the arm binds lands in the pointee, not the selector (`pw_write_through_binding`, 126 and right on 176b); a read-only callee through a held pointer (`pr_local_read`); a holder of a sibling field whose type reads as a holder (`pf_field_other`, an enum with payloads answers YES, DEF-54).
// The class's other kinds hold no header across a block: `if`, `while`, `when`, `loop`, `till`, a bare block (`k_*`, the twins' file); a `defer` body is judged for its block's end (`d1_defer_view`, `d2_defer_lit`).
mod:block_held_view;
error:E5;
